  "heading": "P \\.iff./ Q",
  "heading_latex": "P\\textrm{ if and only if }Q\\textrm{ }P\\textrm{ iff }Q\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{P \\iff Q}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[P \\.iff./ Q]\nStates:\nwhen: P, Q is \\\\statement\nthat:\n. have: P\n  iff: Q\nDocumented:\n. called:\n  . \"$P?$ if and only if $Q?$\"\n  . \"$P?$ iff $Q?$\"\n. written: \"P? \\iff Q?\"\n. description: \"The biconditional of $P$ and $Q$, read *$P$ if and only if $Q$*.\n                It holds exactly when $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth value --\n                each implies the other -- and it is the connective used to state\n                that two conditions are equivalent.\"\nId: \"96440ac7-3331-4467-a7ac-593dbca0761b\"",
